            <ArticleTitle>Giant coronary artery pseudoaneurysm causing pulmonary artery obstruction: a rare complication of coronary bypass surgery--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1073-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report the diagnosis and successful management of a 57-year-old man with right ventricular outflow tract obstruction from a large pseudoaneurysm of the left anterior descending coronary artery 5 years after he had undergone redo coronary artery bypass grafting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
